{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1767447,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"pink_un","paid":0,"title":"Line-O-Mania","festival_id":521405,"organization_id":105898,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-05T00:00:31+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-25T15:30:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"hackathons","public_url":"hackathons\/line-o-mania-tantrafiesta26-iiitn-1767447","region":"offline","details":"<p><span class=\"a_GcMg font-feature-liga-off font-feature-clig-off font-feature-calt-off text-decoration-none text-strikethrough-none\">Line-O-Mania is a robotics contest where teams build autonomous robot capable of following a pre-defined path on a contrast background. The track will be black and white and include challenges such as bends, loop, sharp turns, junctions, dotted lines, and dead-ends. The bots will require precise navigation to reach the end point in the shortest possible time. In addition, a special element will be introduced in the track, which will be disclosed only on the day of the event, adding an extra layer of challenge and unpredictibility.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><strong>Team Formation Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>One participant cannot be in more than one team.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Each team must have a unique team name.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>No restriction on the number of teams from a college.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Inter-college teams are allowed.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Only one member selected by the team will be allowed to perform hand touch to the bot (if required)&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Each team must appoint a Team Leader (all communication via leader).&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Team Leader must be present during the run.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Track Specifications:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Track layout will be disclosed on the spot.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Line: 3cm wide on black and white contrast track.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Start and end points will be different.<\/li>\n<li>Track material: Flex sheets made of PVC<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Bot Specifications:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Robots must be completely autonomous, no remote controlled bots allowed.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Pre-run inspection will be conducted.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>No pneumatics, hydraulics, or harmful mechanisms allowed.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li><strong>No pre-made kits <\/strong>or Lego kits permitted.<\/li>\n<li>Maximum DC voltage &le; 12V between any two circuit points.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>If the bot malfunctions, a short repair timeout of 30 secs can be opted for. Runtime will resume after 30 seconds or whenever the team is ready.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Conduction Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Damaging the arena will lead to instant disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>If the bot leaves the track or requires intervention &rarr; restart from the previous checkpoint. Only <strong>Five (5)<\/strong> such penalties are allowed. <strong>After the 5th penalty the bot will get disqualified.<\/strong><\/li>\n<li>1 minute allowed for sensor calibration before run; timer starts regardless after this.<\/li>\n<li>Violation of rules may lead to disqualification.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>The judge's decision will be final and binding.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<li>Misbehaviour will lead to immediate disqualification.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Judging &amp; Scoring:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Scoring System: (600 - Time taken in seconds) - (Penalties + Skips)<\/li>\n<li>Bonus points for completing the track.<\/li>\n<li>Skipped checkpoints = time penalty<\/li>\n<li>Maximum 2 figures\/obstacles can be skipped; beyond that, all figures\/obstacles have to be cleared or the team may choose to end their run.<\/li>\n<li>If the bot exits the arena, the team will have to restart from their last checkpoint with a penalty.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":"Offering a prize pool of \u20b925,000!!!","regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":2087901,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-07T19:44:17+05:30","updated